---
description: Best practices when interacting with databases in backend Go code.
globs: sql/*.sql, app/internal/**/entities/**/*.go, app/internal/**/repositories/**/*.go
alwaysApply: false
---

The project uses PostgreSQL, the Bun ORM for Go, and Flyway for migrations.

When interacting with databases:

- Keep SQL migrations in `sql/`; follow the existing naming convention for new migrations; do not edit applied migrations—add a new migration to change schema; format migration files.
- Each table maps to a Bun model in the **owning domain module**: `app/internal/<module>/entities/` (for example `app/internal/auth/entities/user.go`).
- The SQL/data-access layer for that domain lives in `app/internal/<module>/repositories/` (for example `app/internal/auth/repositories/user_repository.go`).
- Use prepared statements / Bun query APIs to avoid SQL injection; handle errors explicitly.
- Use connection pooling via the shared DB setup; close resources appropriately.
- Use Taskfile tasks (`migrate`, `clean-migrate`, `clean-migrate-test`) for database lifecycle.
